  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6A81C1">Remark <span data-tag="6A81C1">3.2.5.16</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small category, let $S = \Nerve (\calC )^{op}$, and let $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ be the counit map. For every $\overline{X} = (X,M) \in (\Set ^{+}_{\Delta })_{/\Nerve (\calC )}$, the morphism $\alpha _{\calC }(X): St_{\phi }(X^{op}) \rightarrow {\mathfrak F}_{X}(\calC )^{op}$ of Remark <a href="/tag/4B3BDF" data-tag="4B3BDF">3.2.5.10</a> induces a natural transformation $St^{+}_{\phi } \overline{X}^{op} \rightarrow {\mathfrak F}^{+}_{ \overline{X}}(\calC )^{op}$, which we will denote by $\alpha ^{+}_{\calC }( \overline{X})$. We will regard the collection of morphisms $\{  \alpha ^{+}_{\calC }( \overline{X}) \} _{ \overline{X} \in (\Set ^{+}_{\Delta })_{/\Nerve (\calC )}}$ as determining a natural transformation of functors </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ \alpha _{\calC }: St^{+}_{\phi }( \bullet ^{op}) \rightarrow {\mathfrak F}^{+}_{\bullet }(\calC )^{op}. \]
</div>
</article>